cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AEGIS in a classroom, a curriculum, or a publication, please cite it as below."
title: "AEGIS — Networking Labs for the Classroom"
abstract: >-
  AEGIS turns a single Linux host into a small, self-contained networking lab bench.
  Students get real FRR and Nokia SR Linux routers and switches in a browser tab, with
  an automated grader that scores their configuration against the live devices. It ships
  two labs (demo-01-two-pcs-and-a-real-switch-unsolved and
  demo-02-two-switches-one-router-unsolved) and covers static routing and L2 switching
  only — no OSPF, BGP, EVPN, or VPNs.
type: software
authors:
